  "notes": "Round 1 (fascia: dark wall zone above 3.0 m on the restaurant spans only; mural on 24th Street and both east end faces): one-storey corner fast-food restaurant, SE corner of 24th Street and Mission Street. Flat roof behind a plain parapet. The 24th Street face is a blank stucco wall carrying a large painted mural over its east two-thirds; the glazed dining room, entrance and dark vertical timber-slat cladding sit at the Mission Street end and wrap the corner onto the Mission Street face. Signage kind only: a dark fascia band with a channel-letter wordmark (no text modelled). Round 3 (send-back r1): boxed dark fascia with a light ledge and abstract channel-letter blocks (no text) on 24th and Mission, red boxed canopies over both doors, a lit yellow logo panel, brick-running-bond piers in place of glazed tile, dark storefront glazing, white membrane roof with rooftop plant, a dense painted mural (mural.detail), fast-food menu boards + counter + more dining, interior lights x0.55. Round 5 (send-back r2): stroke-glyph channel letters (generic, spell nothing) on the 24th fascia, lit generic ring-and-disc emblems (no logo shape) (Mission fascia centre, 24th end-bay timber), vertical timber battens (slatCladding) on both end bays and the corner pier, redder tile panels, wider Mission display windows with lit poster panels and a wider glazed double door, clear low-iron shop and door glass so the lit dining room reads, a continuous 0.26 m bright trim band, a light parapet coping cap, and figurative painted forms (faces, hair, raised arms) running up to the parapet over the dense mural tiers (generic, not a copy of the artwork). Round 5 also: doorVignettes - a lit menu-board row on a red wall, a service counter and two-tops seen through each glazed door. Door glass is kit shop glass with a dark frame, meeting stile and push bar.",
